benchscale bundles no third-party files.

It links to these projects. src/benchscale/data/thirdparty.json names the files
it uses at pinned upstream commits; they are downloaded from GitHub on first use
into a local cache (~/.cache/benchscale), under their own licences:

Opentrons labware definitions
  Source:  https://github.com/Opentrons/opentrons/tree/edge/shared-data/labware/definitions/2
  Licence: Apache License 2.0 - Copyright 2015-2025 Opentrons Labworks, Inc.
  Use:     benchscale reads outer sizes and well positions to build its reference library.

Prompt to Bench design library
  Source:  https://github.com/ATinyGreenCell/prompt-to-bench
  Licence: CERN-OHL-P-2.0 for the designs (see that repository)

Dimensions of tubes, slides, pipette tips and the microplate footprint in
src/benchscale/data/standards.json are facts taken from the manufacturer and
standards documents cited on each entry.
